OL,3,AMore than #2m spent by government on
OL,4,Ainfluencers since July 2024
OL,5,
OL,6,FGovernment departments have disclosed
OL,7,Fthat they have spent at least #2.4m
OL,8,Fworking with social media influencers
OL,9,Fsince July 2024.
OL,11,FDepartments have used influencers to
OL,12,Fpromote campaigns on topics including
OL,13,Fcareer development, how to access
OL,14,Fbenefits, as well as recruitment of
OL,15,Fteachers and prison officers.
OL,17,FOf those providing figures, the
OL,18,FDepartment for Education (DfE) has
OL,19,Fspent the most at more than #700,000,
OL,20,Ffollowed by HMRC, which has spent
OL,21,Fnearly #600,000, although this excludes
OL,22,Fagency fees.
OL,23,APub: 16-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
